<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Robeson returns six weeks after starting sertraline. He took 50 mg for two weeks with mild nausea that passed in a week, and after the nurse&apos;s phone check he has taken 100 mg for three and a half weeks. He has been to five behavioral activation sessions and has begun short walks and an hour of reading each day, but he still wakes early, has little pleasure, and has not sung. He has had no thoughts of being better off dead for three weeks. He has noticed no rise in energy or reduced need for sleep. He takes every dose and keeps his medicines locked. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg for two weeks, then 100 mg for three and a half weeks; every dose taken</td></tr><tr><td>Therapy</td><td>Five behavioral activation sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 19 from 22; no thoughts of death for three weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Side effects</td><td>Nausea in the first week only</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

