  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Recurrent major depression on sertraline (F33.2)</content>. PHQ-9 22 to 19 at six weeks: a minimal response, with three and a half weeks at 100 mg. The dose can go higher before the trial is judged. Sodium 138, normal. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide for three weeks; medicines locked; 988 in his phone. No signs of hypomania. [S]<list><item>Sertraline 150 mg each morning from today, then 200 mg in two weeks if tolerated.</item><item>Continue weekly behavioral activation.</item><item>Review in seven weeks, when he will have had about five weeks at 200 mg.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9</td><td>Baseline and at least monthly during acute treatment (CMID)</td><td>Completed today</td><td>19, down 14 percent from 22; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9 between visits, rated by the psychologist at each session</td><td>At each therapy session</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed: no PHQ-9 was collected about four weeks into treatment; the two-week nurse call checked side effects and safety but not the PHQ-9, and no visit was booked at four weeks. No harm judging by today&apos;s score and his safety review. Corrective action: the psychologist now rates the PHQ-9 at each weekly session and reports any rise or positive item 9 the same day</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Suicide-risk review (C-SSRS screen since the last visit), safety plan, locked medicines and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</td><td>Every visit during active treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No thoughts of suicide for three weeks; medicines locked; safety plan reviewed</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Sodium (SSRI or SNRI in an older adult)</td><td>Baseline, about four to six weeks after starting, and with symptoms</td><td>Completed today</td><td>138 mmol/L, normal</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and adverse-effect review</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Every dose taken; nausea in the first week only</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adequacy of the antidepressant trial (dose and duration)</td><td>At each review: at least four to eight weeks at an adequate dose before judging response</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Three and a half weeks at 100 mg: not yet an adequate trial; dose raised</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Watch for hypomania or mixed features after starting or changing an antidepressant</td><td>Every visit; repeat the MDQ if features emerge</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No elation, reduced need for sleep or racing thoughts</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Behavioral activation with a psychologist</td><td>Weekly for about sixteen sessions</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Five sessions attended; daily walks and reading scheduled</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Trust, confidentiality and culturally responsive care</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>He feels able to speak freely with his therapist</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Social work for income and costs</td><td>Monthly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Meeting the social worker monthly about costs</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Response to treatment: PHQ-9 down by at least half from 22. In progress; target 1957-10-05 [S]</item><item>Remission: PHQ-9 below 5. In progress; target 1957-10-05 [S]</item><item>Stay safe: safety plan in place and reviewed at every visit, with no self-harm. In progress; target 1957-10-05 [S]</item><item>Sing again: daily vocal practice and one public engagement a month. In progress; target 1957-10-05 [S]</item><item>Sleep six to seven hours a night. In progress; target 1957-10-05 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: APA Clinical Practice Guideline for the Treatment of Depression Across Three Age Cohorts (2019); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Williams DR, et al. Prevalence and distribution of major depressive disorder in African Americans, Caribbean blacks, and non-Hispanic whites: results from the National Survey of American Life. Arch Gen Psychiatry 2007;64(3):305-315 (2007)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Sertraline 200 mg in two weeks. Review in seven weeks with the PHQ-9 and sodium. Weekly behavioral activation with a PHQ-9 at each session. Call or text 988 at any time in a crisis. Next scheduled visit 1957-06-08: three-month review: no response to an adequate sertraline trial; switch to venlafaxine. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
